<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hausa Bakwai</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> Bakwai are the seven 'true' Hausa states of tradition: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daura">Daura</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a>, Katsina, Zazzau, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gobir">Gobir</a>, Rano and Biram, said to descend from the legendary hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayajidda">Bayajidda</a> and his offspring. They are contrasted with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banza-bakwai">Banza Bakwai</a>, seven 'illegitimate' states. The scheme reflects later political tradition rather than a historical federation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hausa-bakwai.jpg" alt="Hausa Bakwai" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zykasaa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AFRhausalandas.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
